              <div class="report-heading">USG Abdomen & Pelvis (Male)</div>
              <div class="report-body-text">STUDY: ULTRASONOGRAPHY OF WHOLE ABDOMEN & PELVIS (MALE)

FINDINGS:
- LIVER: Normal in size (13.8 cm) and shape. Echotexture is homogeneous. No focal parenchymal lesion, cyst, or IHBRD noted.
- GALL BLADDER: Well-distended with clear lumen. Normal wall thickness (2.3 mm). No calculus or mass lesion.
- COMMON BILE DUCT (CBD): Normal in caliber (3.6 mm).
- PANCREAS: Normal in size, contour, and echogenicity. MPD is not dilated.
- SPLEEN: Normal in size (9.8 cm) with uniform parenchymal echotexture.
- KIDNEYS:
  * Right Kidney: Measures 10.4 cm. Normal cortical thickness and echogenicity. No calculus or hydronephrosis.
  * Left Kidney: Measures 10.6 cm. Normal cortical thickness and echogenicity. No calculus or hydronephrosis.
- URINARY BLADDER: Well-distended with smooth mucosal margins. Lumen clear.
- PROSTATE: Normal in size, measuring 3.6 x 3.2 x 3.0 cm (Approx weight: 18 grams). Homogeneous parenchymal echotexture. Capsular margin is intact. Post-void residual (PVR) urine volume is insignificant.
- PERITONEAL CAVITY: No ascites or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.</div>

              <div class="impression-block">
